' Order-then-execute for cost-accounted (v6) shards, with record and replay
' (amendment of 2026-10-13). Consensus orders accepted envelopes and never
' waits for execution. One executor runs each finalized block, applies the P1
' gate before each envelope, settles, and publishes its record. Every other
' node replays that record. Replay follows the record, so honest replays of
' one record reach one root, whether the reduction scheduler stays or goes and
' whether the candidate pick is fixed or random. A wrong attestation or an
' invalid record is shown by replaying the record.
'
' Paper anchors: P1 = publications cost-accounting/cost-accounted-rho.tex
'   gate P1:2188-2213 · rejection without effect P1:2208-2212 ·
'   block validity P1:1708-1714 · the run decides P1:2090-2093 ·
'   refund from the actual run P1:2154-2160.
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-consensus-proposal.md §7.
' It supersedes the diagram consensus-proposal-order-then-execute.puml, which
' assumed a deterministic executor. That diagram stays for the record.
' Palette: user and envelope = supply blue · proposer = control amber ·
'   Casper core = capability indigo · linearizer = process lilac ·
'   executor = pool green · replay = surface salmon ·
'   records and executed roots = delta orange · evidence = reject red
' The legend also defines every name and abbreviation that the labels use,
' so the diagram reads on its own.
' Render:  ./render.sh consensus-proposal-record-and-replay.puml

@startuml consensus-proposal-record-and-replay
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor              $ca_neutral
  LifeLineBorderColor     #666666
  ParticipantBorderColor  #333333
  DividerBackgroundColor  $ca_note_grey
  GroupBorderColor        #666666
  GroupBackgroundColor    #FAFAFA
}
skinparam maxMessageSize 340
title Order-then-execute on v6 shards with record and replay (amendment of 2026-10-13)
footer DR-131: host-work metering is removed (75de2dc39). The host-work parts of this diagram are historical.

autonumber

actor       "User\n(signer)"                                as U $ca_supply
participant "Proposer\n(no execution)"                       as P $ca_control
participant "Validators\n(structural validity)"              as V $ca_capability
participant "Fork choice and\nclique-oracle finality"        as F $ca_capability
participant "Linearizer\n(main-chain epochs)"                as L $ca_process
participant "Executor of block b\n(by convention, the sender of b)" as X $ca_pool
participant "Every other node\n(replays the record)"         as R $ca_surface
database    "Records and\nexecuted roots"                    as A $ca_delta

== Inclusion and structural validation: as in the first version ==
U -[$ca_instantiate]> P : signed offered envelope
P -> A : newest finalized block E whose canonical record\nthis node has replayed, and its root <latex>r_E</latex>
P -> P : inclusion filter at <latex>r_E</latex>: DR-64 check,\nDR-65 group rule, per-block demand cap
P -[$ca_instantiate]> V : block = parents, justifications, envelopes,\nattestation <latex>(E, r_E)</latex>, epoch validator set,\nand the records that this node executed and no earlier block cites
V -> V : signatures, justifications, equivocation, envelope rules,\nrecord encoding, each cited block lies in the past cone
V -> F : add the valid block to the DAG
note over P, F $ca_note_green
  **Consensus keeps accepting blocks.** No step of inclusion
  or validation waits for execution or for replay
  (P1:1708-1714 makes block validity a syntactic predicate).
end note

== Finality and linearization: unchanged ==
F -> F : LMD-GHOST fork choice, clique oracle with the epoch weights
F -> L : the LFB advances: the newly finalized set
L -> X : block b in the canonical order Ord, envelopes in block order
L -> R : the same order Ord (every node runs the linearizer)

== Execution: one executor runs block b and records it ==
loop each envelope e of b, in block order
  X -> X : P1 gate at the current root: <latex>\Sigma_s \geq \Delta_s</latex> for every lane s?\n(DR-65 group rule inside b)
  alt the gate accepts
    X -> X : hold, execute, settle, fee to the sender of b
  else the gate rejects
    X -[$ca_debit]> X : reject e: no state change, no tokens consumed (P1:2208-2212)
  end
end
X -> X : <latex>\mathrm{rec}(b)</latex> = pre-root, gate verdicts, processed deploys\n(event log, native cost evidence), system work, post-root
X -> X : certify <latex>\mathrm{rec}(b)</latex> by one replay, as today's producer does
X -[$ca_instantiate]> V : cite <latex>\mathrm{rec}(b)</latex> in the executor's next block
note over X $ca_note_amber
  The run is one valid run among many:
  a random candidate pick, and, with or without
  the scheduler, any order that the rules allow
  (P1:2090-2093). The record fixes the run.
end note

== Replay: every other node follows the record ==
F -> R : a block that cites <latex>\mathrm{rec}(b)</latex> is finalized
R -> A : fix the canonical record of b:\nthe first citation of b in Ord that starts at <latex>\mathrm{executed}(\mathrm{prev}(b))</latex>\nand replays to its stated post-root
R -> R : replay <latex>\mathrm{rec}(b)</latex>:\nthe recorded COMMs,\nthe same host work in every replay
alt replay fails, or ends at another root
  R -[$ca_debit]> A : signed invalid-record evidence against the citing sender,\nthen try the next citation in Ord
else replay reaches the stated root
  R -> A : <latex>\mathrm{executed}(b)</latex> = the post-root of the canonical record
end

== Attestation and dispute ==
P -[$ca_instantiate]> V : a later block attests <latex>(E', r_{E'})</latex>
V -> A : when replay reaches <latex>E'</latex>:\ncompare <latex>r_{E'}</latex> with <latex>\mathrm{executed}(E')</latex>,\nand re-run the inclusion filter of that block at <latex>r_{E'}</latex>
note over V, A $ca_note_red
  A root mismatch, an invalid record, or an envelope that fails
  the filter at the proposer's own attested root is signed slashing
  evidence. Any node proves it by replaying the records.
  It never changes block validity after the fact.
end note

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| user and signed envelope |
  |<$ca_control>| proposer |
  |<$ca_capability>| Casper core: validity, DAG, fork choice, finality |
  |<$ca_process>| deterministic linearization of finalized blocks |
  |<$ca_pool>| the one executor of a block, which records the run |
  |<$ca_surface>| replay of the record on every other node |
  |<$ca_delta>| records and executed roots |
  |<$ca_note_red>| slashing evidence |

  |= name |= meaning |
  | P1 | the paper "Cost-Accounted Rho Calculus" (L. G. Meredith, May 2026). P1:a-b cites its lines a to b. |
  | P1 gate | accept an envelope only if <latex>\Sigma_s \geq \Delta_s</latex> for every signature lane s |
  | <latex>\Sigma_s</latex>, <latex>\Delta_s</latex> | the token supply and the demand of signature s |
  | DR-64, DR-65 | the decision records of the funding check before execution, and of same-block offers on one purse |
  | E, <latex>r_E</latex> | the newest finalized block whose canonical record the proposer has replayed, and the root after it. E' is a later one. |
  | b, e | one finalized block, and one envelope (a signed user deploy) of it |
  | Ord, prev(b) | the canonical order of finalized blocks, and the block before b in it |
  | <latex>\mathrm{rec}(b)</latex> | the record of one run of b: pre-root, verdicts, processed deploys, system work, post-root |
  | <latex>\mathrm{executed}(b)</latex> | the post-root of the canonical record of b |
  | canonical record | the first record of b that a finalized block cites in Ord, starts at executed(prev(b)) and replays to its stated root |
  | COMM | one RSpace communication event: a send that matches a receive |
  | LMD-GHOST | latest-message-driven greedy heaviest-observed subtree fork choice |
  | LFB, DAG | the last finalized block, and the directed acyclic graph of blocks |
  | v6 | protocol version 6, with cost accounting and offered envelopes |
endlegend

@enduml
